{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter's Graduation", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Finally!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressions of Time", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use transition words or connectors to indicate when something happened or was happening. <br><br> These connectors are often followed by the Simple Past tense. They help say when something happened.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Expression\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"as soon as\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"without delay; quickly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yesterday\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"on the day before this one\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"after\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"afterward; later \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"before\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"previous to; earlier or sooner than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"at the moment\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"whenever\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"every time;  any time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meanwhile\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"at or during the same time\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "She said she would call as soon as she knew.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Whenever I saw a food magazine, I thought of you cooking.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past tense  versus  Past Continuous tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. <br> You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular. <br> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied</span>. <br> Irregular verbs change in different ways. <br>For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask\u2026?</span>  <br> <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For Past Continuous, we add was/were + verb\u201cing\u201d to verbs. Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add \u201cing\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" was/were talking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were getting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"flew\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" was/were flying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"work\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"worked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were working\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discuss\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discussed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were discussing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"enjoy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"enjoyed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were enjoying\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Did she tell you when she was flying home?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She said she was getting ready to come back.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "as soon as", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in the shortest possible time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(connector)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Call me as soon as you get home! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about school and work life.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meanwhile ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "while another thing is happening ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was working. Meanwhile, he was at the beach having fun. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to discuss", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk about", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We discussed many different topics. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le13ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content":